{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe infra/terraform cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/terraform/acm.tf:1-7,40-44` — Preserve adopted wildcard cert, DNS validation records drive renewal, `prevent_destroy`, direct ARN consumers. Consumer: Terraform operators.\n- `infra/terraform/iam_bridge_metrics.tf:1-27,82-85` — Preserve separate repo-scoped role, only `PutMetricData`, namespace condition despite wildcard resource, output copied to repository variable. Consumer: Terraform/security/operators.\n- `infra/terraform/iam_s2.tf:1-26` — Preserve reuse existing instance role/SSM permissions; no additional IAM; future grants attach to the existing role. Consumer: Terraform/security maintainers.\n- `infra/terraform/iam_s4a.tf:1-34` — Preserve no additional IAM; existing `/rebar/prod/*` read covers token; workstation writes do not use instance role; do not redeclare role data. Consumer: Terraform/security maintainers.\n- `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf:1-56` — Preserve existing-role attachment, Claude-only resource scope, Converse authorizes through `InvokeModel`, profile plus underlying models required, streaming action required, region/profile wildcard rationale. Consumer: Terraform/security/Bedrock operators.\n- `infra/terraform/iam.tf:1-11,101-105,130-143` — Preserve single instance/DLM role ownership, downstream scoped policies, read-only GitHub OIDC trust and required KMS-via-SSM exception. Consumer: Terraform/security review.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_1fa8.tf:1-49,68-83` — Preserve alarm covers host-observable dispatch leg, metric is dimensionless/unconditional, 2-of-3 jitter tolerance, missing data breaches, SNS actions. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_88ab.tf:1-34,51-66` — Preserve metric source/meaning, evaluation window, unconditional-zero publisher, missing-data policy, notification. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_9ea3.tf:1-36,67-79` — Preserve signal contract, threshold/window, dead-publisher semantics, why this cadence differs if behaviorally necessary. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:1-26,43-59,72-120,141-156,188-229,265-277` — Preserve each metric’s source, cadence-aligned threshold, dead-publisher treatment, distinct deferral/unreachable/persistent-pressure conditions, notifications. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_bridge.tf:1-50,71-82` — Preserve dimensionless hourly 0/1 metric, two consecutive failures, missing data non-breaching because heartbeat canary owns stopped runs, SNS actions. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:1-58,80-120,222-225` — Preserve metric expressions and divide-by-zero/idle guards, thresholds, two-way SNS, discoverability locals. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_foxterrier.tf:1-45,71-75,112-116` — Preserve MCP deployment-health signals, periods/thresholds, unconditional publisher, missing-data breach, notifications. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf:1-34,56-93` — Preserve voter-error metric source, sustained-failure shape, dead-publisher behavior, both alarm and recovery notifications. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_s5.tf:1-29,44-70` — Preserve failure metric, 2-of-3 window, missing-data breach, alarm/OK notifications. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_ws7.tf:1-24,40-57` — Preserve sustained mirror divergence, evaluation window, unconditional publisher, missing-data policy, notifications. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring.tf:1-30,55-65,170-176,200-216,230-249,261-304` — Preserve shared SNS, metric sources/dimensions, dead-publisher behavior, data-volume/debris alarm thresholds, DLM assertion. Consumer: Terraform/CloudWatch operators.\n- `infra/terraform/oidc.tf:1-12` — Preserve account-singleton GitHub OIDC provider is now owned here and required by the drift role; imported rather than recreated. Consumer: Terraform/security.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by the row-by-row completion comment.\n- [ ] Every consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by the row-by-row completion comment.\n- [ ] No executable behavior changes; verified by inspecting the final diff and running the command under Verification.\n- [ ] No test assertion changes; verified by inspecting the final diff.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788586829209245001,"uuid":"22366834-46c9-4f88-b5e6-ce2639cf4257"}